Description:
    Generates a new database migration. Pass the migration name, either
    CamelCased or under_scored, and an optional list of attribute pairs as arguments.

    A migration class is generated in db/migrate prefixed by a timestamp of the current date and time.

    You can name your migration in either of these formats to generate add/remove
    column lines from supplied attributes: add_{columns}_to_{table} or remove_{columns}_from_{table}.

    A migration name containing JoinTable will generate join tables for use with
    hasAndBelongsToMany associations.

    You can also name your migration create_{table} along with any attributes to generate a regular table.

Examples:
    `bin/trails generate migration add_ssl_flag`

    If the current date is May 14, 2008 and the current time 09:09:12, this creates the AddSslFlag migration
    db/migrate/20080514090912_add_ssl_flag.ts

    `bin/trails generate migration add_title_body_published_to_post title:string body:text published:boolean`

    This will create db/migrate/20080514090912_add_title_body_published_to_post.ts with this in the migration:

      await this.addColumn("posts", "title", "string");
      await this.addColumn("posts", "body", "text");
      await this.addColumn("posts", "published", "boolean");

    `bin/trails generate migration create_media_join_table artists musics:uniq`

    This will create a join table migration:

    await this.createJoinTable("artists", "musics", (t) => {
      // t.index(["artist_id", "music_id"]);
      t.index(["music_id", "artist_id"], { unique: true });
    });

    `bin/trails generate migration create_users email:string`

    This will create the migration:

    await this.createTable("users", (t) => {
      t.string("email");
      t.timestamps();
    });
